{
  "name": "Building materials",
  "icon": "slimic:slimic_stone_bricks",
  "category": "slimic:world",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The Slimic Blocks tab has 32 base materials, 8 stairs, 8 slabs and 6 walls. Gather stone and soft materials in The Slimic with suitable tools; Slimic Stone drops Slimic Cobblestone without Silk Touch. Cut masonry with a stonecutter or craft shaped pieces. A hoe tills Slimic Soil, Damp Grass or Slime Mud with clear space above into farmland."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Craft 2×2 squares of Slimic Stone, Ancient Foundation, Slime Marble or Slimic Slate into matching bricks. Pale or black stone makes polished stone; stone bricks make tiles. Four blocks yield four. Add vines or a moss block for mossy cobblestone or bricks. Stack two stone-brick or marble slabs vertically for one chiseled block."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Smelt Slimic Cobblestone into Slimic Stone, stone bricks or tiles into cracked forms, Slime Silt into Gel Glass, and Congealed Slime into Dried Slime. Mix planks or clay with a slimeball for infused planks or Slimic Clay. Congealed Slime and a clay ball make Hardened Slime."
    }
  ],
